  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S Nirma Ltd. vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 19 May, 2025 Author: Vishal Mishra Bench: Vishal Mishra Neutral Citation No. 2025:Mphc-Jbp:24593 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Vishal Mishra On The 19th Of May, 2025 Misc. Criminal Case No. 20075 of 2025 M/S Nirma Ltd. Versus The State Of Madhya Pradesh",
    "facts": "The applicant has filed the present application under Section 482 of Cr.P.C. for seeking modification of order dated 15.05.2024 passed in M.Cr.C No.42949/2021. 2. It is the case of the applicant that the applicant is facing trial in the Court of CJM, Satna for offences punishable under Sections 7(1)/16,7(i1i)/16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act 1954 (for short 'the Act of 1954'). The same was rejected by the learned trial Court which was challenged by filing M.Cr.C. No.42949/2021. Therefore, this application is filed seeking modification of the order passed by this Court on 15.05.2021.",
    "arguments": "It is argued that the M/S Nirma Ltd. vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 19 May, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/5636812/ 1 learned CJM is pointing out that there was no direction by the Hon'ble High Court for imposition of cost during the summary proceedings and disposal of the matter. 4. However the fact remains that the Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Nemichand Jain (supra)",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "It is argued that the M/S Nirma Ltd. vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 19 May, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/5636812/ 1 learned CJM is pointing out that there was no direction by the Hon'ble High Court for imposition of cost during the summary proceedings and disposal of the matter. 4. However the fact remains that the Hon'ble Supreme Court in the case of Nemichand Jain (supra)"
  },
